WEBVTT

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.370
<i>Capeta!</i>

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:07.740
<i>Capeta...</i>

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.990
<i>He did it!</i>

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.560
<i>45-second range!</i>

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.050
<i>T-Taira's also...!</i>

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.050
<i>N-No way!</i>

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:28.710
<b>Final session, finished!</b>

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.980
Now then.  #14, Suzuki Monami-san.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:40.980
Please tell us, is there a singer you admire or an artist you hold as a role model?

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.540
Who are you aiming for?

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.650
No one in particular.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:46.860
<i>Monami?</i>

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.750
The only thing I want to do is make everyone happy.

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:57.170
Or rather, you'll all be happy if I cheer for you.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.400
We were going through some hard times,
 but I cheered everyone on and pulled us forward.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.350
That's why we were able to come this far.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:08.890
Um...  You...  W-What are you talking about?

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:12.560
That's why I'll keep on cheering!

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.350
Not just for Ca-chan or Nobu, but for more people!

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.980
That's why I decided to become a singer!

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.450
I want to make everyone happy with my singing!

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.140
<i>She's gone and done it...</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.170
Once again it seems you didn't practice beforehand.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:38.560
Yes.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.710
This is my first time driving on a long course like this one.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:47.820
Until the final session this afternoon, when I could attack with new tires...

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.530
I tried my best at everything I could do.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:52.720
I see.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.180
So you won't have any regrets about the final result then?

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:57.890
Yes.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:01.060
Still, I wanted to race more...

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:04.270
on this circuit, with that machine...

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:07.090
because it was really fun.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:11.220
Because of that, I'm not at all satisfied!

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:53.680
Please excuse me.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:07.890
It's Shiba Ryou.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:08.740
If you'll excuse me.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:09.880
Come in.

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:15.670
<i>I want to race.</i>

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.660
<i>I want to race here more!</i>

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:24.230
<i>I don't want it to end here!</i>

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:27.430
My aim is the F1.

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:29.000
Please let me drive your works machine!

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:30.670
Please!

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:34.930
<i>Please!</i>

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.680
<i>Let him pass somehow!</i>

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:39.580
<i>Capeta.</i>

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:48.320
A guy driving on this circuit for the first time got 1 minute 45.913 seconds?!

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.100
They must have timed it wrong.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.430
That has to be it.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:57.060
Do you really think a Grade 1 circuit that hosts F1 races would make a mistake with the time?

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.230
But I can't believe it.

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:03.370
That two people would get the same time up to 0.001 of a second.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.290
The facts are the facts.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.500
And which one are you going to take?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.780
I'm sure you've already decided.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.510
Let's see what the works team decides first.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:17.470
I suppose it's Shiba.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:21.430
Simply looking at it, there's no complaining about his records so far, but...

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.220
Yeah.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.940
In that case, Taira also...!

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:28.480
That's right, he got the same time as Shiba.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:33.440
But he wrecked a car while at the school...

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:36.170
Is that such a big deal?

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:38.870
Crashes happen in races.

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:41.380
No.  Crashes aren't good.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:43.040
If you crash during a race,

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:46.320
not only will you not win nor stand on top of the podium, but you won't earn points either.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.670
It's the same as not participating in that race.

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:49.750
That's right.

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:55.630
That's why we don't take those who don't produce results at FSRS, even if they are fast.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:58.410
But it sure is a waste.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:04.030
Letting go of a boy who posted a time rivaling Ishihara's on his first race on this circuit...

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.490
Which do you want, Tanaka-san?!

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:08.100
Are you accepting Taira?!

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:13.720
Whether crashing is forbidden or not,
 wasn't there another rule?

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.320
Weren't we going to take on the one who grew the most during the three days at the school?

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:28.250
<b>I will now announce the results.</b>

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:32.130
<b>Mvex New Wave, Final Selection.</b>

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:37.550
<b>Out of these 20 candidates lined up here today, the one who will take the crown is...</b>

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:45.770
The successful candidate who will be taking this year's FSRS scholarship is...

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:54.760
<b>Entry #3.  Yamamoto Mina-san!</b>

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.700
The successful candidate is...

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:03.570
Shiba Ryou.

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:06.320
All right!

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:16.200
In the end, we narrowed it down to two candidates.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.810
There was a split among the staff, but...

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:24.430
it was finally decided by me,
as the chief manager of the team.

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:32.390
Not only is Shiba able to constantly drive fast, but he can be relied on to finish the race.

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:35.280
For this reason...

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:37.410
<i>Reliability...</i>

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:42.410
<i>That means drivers who crash aren't good.</i>

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:45.240
<i>I can't become a professional just by being fast.</i>

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:52.100
<i>Unless I can finish for certain, I won't have the trust of the team and I'll cause trouble for a lot of people.</i>

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:56.560
<i>When you think about it, it's so obvious...</i>

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.970
<i>I'm too late... realizing this now!</i>

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.640
Capeta, how was it?!

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:16.610
I see.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:21.580
Sorry, Nobu, Dad.

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:23.840
You don't need to apologize.

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:27.280
Oh, but you did great!

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:29.530
Your driving was excellent!

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:32.080
Watching you drive gave me goose bumps.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:36.890
Getting that time on your first try on this circuit...

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:39.140
I was... really...

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:40.420
But...

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:42.090
I can't race anymore.

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:46.430
Against Shiba or Minamoto...

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:48.600
And I haven't settled the fight yet.

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:49.690
Capeta.

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:53.100
They can still drive on, but...

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:59.070
our race... is now... finished, Nobu.

00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:00.370
Capeta.

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:05.030
I... wanted... I wanted to race more.

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:06.440
More...

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:10.490
Capeta.

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:24.920
And I... promised you... a chance to fight Minamoto...

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:27.930
I'm sorry, Capeta.

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:29.300
Oh, there you are.

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:30.890
Taira-sa—

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:38.670
That is...

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:40.860
I'm sorry to interrupt you all, but...

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:44.650
I-If it's about the charges for the repairs...

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.820
No, it's not that.

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:50.780
There's something I want to talk with Taira-kun about.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.630
What's with those judges?!

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:56.750
They're blind!

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.210
Please wait, Monami!

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:04.560
I refuse the entertainment world if it doesn't see my worth!

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.390
I said, wait!

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:08.380
Could you hold for a sec?

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:10.390
Yuuji-san?!

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.230
You're Suzuki Monami-san, right?

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:15.100
I was wondering if I could have some of your time.

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:18.800
I would like to talk to you.

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:23.880
<i>That Yuuji-san?!</i>

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:26.350
What?!

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:27.320
You're serious?!

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:34.140
Well, they're a private team participating in Formula Stellar, so they're our rival...

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:38.040
and they're currently looking for a driver.

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:42.650
They seemed to have liked Taira-kun when they saw his driving today.

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:46.010
And they'd like you to consider joining Persec.

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:49.210
Hey, Capeta...

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:52.160
How about it?

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:54.260
Want to drive at Persec-san's place?

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:55.180
Y-Yes!

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:56.310
U-Um...

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:57.660
Please!

00:10:57.860 --> 00:10:59.480
Please!

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:02.260
The scholarship was a shame, but...

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.450
Taira-kun, Andou-kun.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:08.040
You two should do just fine.

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:13.230
We may be taking different paths, but we're all aiming for the same place.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:15.500
Your path may be tough, but do your best.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:17.440
I'll be rooting for you.

00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:18.480
Yes!

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:23.710
Oh.  And I'm counting on you to pay for the repairs, Dad.

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:27.980
Oh yeah.

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:31.410
Tsubomaki-san's place is famous for their Spartan training.

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.340
You should brace yourself.

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:35.390
I'll do my best!

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:36.630
Bye.

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:40.590
Capeta.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:41.820
Nobu.

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:43.400
I can still race...

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:44.980
I'm not finished yet!

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:46.940
Nope.  You're not finished.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.550
Not even in karting.

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:50.870
A-Adachi-san!

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:08.730
<b>Japan National Kart Championship, Final Round.</b>

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:12.450
<b>The qualifying heat for the ICA class is coming to a close.</b>

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:15.150
<b>There's only a couple of laps left.</b>

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:19.840
<b>The point leader in the West district, #1, Sena.</b>

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.980
<b>So far he's been feeling the pressure of defeat.</b>

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:26.490
<b>He can't finish like this.</b>

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:29.150
<b>Now would be a nice time to see his fighting spirit.</b>

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:35.110
<i>When I heard that Shiba from the East district pulled out, I thought this would be a cinch.</i>

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:37.110
<i>But there's a hitch...</i>

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:44.250
<b>So far, the driver dominating the top
 is car #30, Taira Capeta!</b>

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:51.130
<b>The new frame they brought in with this year's season is a perfect match.</b>

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:54.130
<b>He beat the course record on his time attack.</b>

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.050
All right!  Way to go!

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:58.730
Last lap!

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:00.640
Keep it up!

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:03.010
But I sure am surprised.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:07.470
Only the top drivers in the nation can compete in this East-West United Race.

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:09.980
And to think he'd stay at the top through all the races.

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:11.700
Of course!

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:15.450
Capeta was fast, even with that three-year-old frame.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:20.930
And now he's on a new high-spec machine, supplied by a maker.

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:25.840
And now that Shiba went off to the FSte after turning 16...

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:29.250
there's no one who can beat Capeta now!

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:32.870
<i>ICA End-of-Season...</i>

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:34.380
<i>East-West United Round?</i>

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:35.380
<i>That's it!</i>

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:39.830
<i>You've come this far and you're still in a position to win the championship for the series.</i>

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:41.850
<i>It'd be a waste if you didn't compete.</i>

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:43.490
<i>A-Adachi-san.</i>

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:46.930
<i>Why is a reporter for a kart magazine here?</i>

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:51.860
<i>I'm Adachi, the kart otaku who follows Taira Capeta wherever he goes.</i>

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:53.950
<i>So you'll participate, right?</i>

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:58.070
<i>You should know already, Adachi-san.</i>

00:13:58.070 --> 00:14:02.330
<i>Whether we want to participate or not, we don't have the all-important frame.</i>

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.150
<i>You won't have to worry about that.</i>

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:12.340
<i>Harada-san here is proposing to support you.</i>

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:14.260
<i>What?!</i>

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:17.560
<i>I heard that you're still 15.</i>

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:23.760
<i>You can't participate in the FSte until you're 16, so until then, you can compete in kart races, right?</i>

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:25.220
<i>What does that mean?</i>

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:29.190
<i>It means that even if you're going to be working with Persec,</i>

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:32.230
<i>you won't be able to compete in the races until your birthday next year.</i>

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:33.560
<i>Eh?  Is that so?</i>

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:35.230
<i>Even that Minamoto.</i>

00:14:35.230 --> 00:14:37.330
<i>He passed the audition last year,</i>

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:42.230
<i>but continued in karting and didn't compete in the FSte until he turned 16 this year.</i>

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:44.200
<i>Ah.  So that's how it is.</i>

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:48.450
<i>So that's why I'm hoping Taira-kun would drive on our kart...</i>

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:53.710
<i>and compete in the ICA this year and the FA next year.</i>

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:56.210
<i>Are you serious?</i>

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:58.670
<i>Yeah.  We'll fully support you.</i>

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:03.830
<i>It's starting to move...</i>

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:04.980
All right!  Way to go, Capeta!

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:06.520
<i>A lot of things are starting to move.</i>

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:06.520
That's it!  Go!

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:12.230
<i>We didn't get the scholarship, but it was worth aiming for.</i>

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:19.190
<i>It wasn't a mistake, going to see Tanaka-san personally back then.</i>

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:22.010
<b>Now, Taira, who's at his best today,</b>

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:28.120
<b>increases his distance from the rest, turns the last corner, and finishes on top!</b>

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:29.420
All right!

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:31.840
He'll start at pole position in the finals.

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:34.730
His dream has finally come true.

00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:37.610
He always had to outdo himself.

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:43.250
But now my dream of getting him on a new machine has finally...!

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.950
Yeah.  I'm really happy.

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:47.050
Right, Shige-san?

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.050
Yeah.

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:51.550
Nobu worked hard too, but you also did great.

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:56.110
From that crappy kart, made from salvaged scrap...

00:15:56.110 --> 00:15:57.560
It's amazing you all got this far.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.740
I bow my head to you.

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:01.380
O-Oh no...

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:03.950
Don't make me cry, Kumada-san.

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:06.160
What are you all crying for?!

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:09.700
Three men, all crying.  How pathetic!

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:12.080
Can Ca-chan really win with that?!

00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:15.030
W-What's the matter, Monami-chan?

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:18.050
You said you couldn't come today because you had to prepare for your debut, right?

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:19.510
Are you sure it's okay?

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:23.400
Especially when you caught the eye of a popular producer.

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:26.140
Yuuji said I should go.

00:16:26.140 --> 00:16:26.550
Eh?

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:29.240
Voice training, singing, and dancing...

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:34.030
I've been taking lessons continuously, so he told me I should go take a break.

00:16:34.030 --> 00:16:36.560
That's why I hopped on the bullet train and came here.

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:38.750
And what do I find?!

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:40.530
What's with this tight-fisted atmosphere!

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:43.480
There's no time to be crying!

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:45.290
Put more spirit into it!

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:46.680
Damn it!

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:48.950
But this time there's no part that we can play.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:48.950
Stop crying!  Damn it!

00:16:53.410 --> 00:16:55.030
How is it?

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.750
Is there anything that's bothering you, like the balance of the frame?

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:00.660
I don't think there's any problem with the balance,

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:03.670
but it's so stable that it's hard to make the turns on the corners.

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:07.830
I'd find it easier to enter the corners and turn,
 if it lost some of the stability.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:09.300
All right.  Got it.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:12.300
Wow...  It doesn't look like our team.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.020
Yeah.

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:16.990
Capeta-kun's finally showing his true strength.

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:18.300
Manager Nanako.

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:22.990
But from my point of view, the manufacturers sure took their time noticing.

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:28.780
With so much talent, he should have had more support earlier.

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:33.950
You saw Capeta-kun had talent five years ago, right?

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:37.500
But that boy came this far on his own strength.

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:38.350
Capeta!  Show us a great race!

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:39.200
He may have taken the long route,

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:44.340
but he convinced everyone around him with his talent and got hold of his position now.

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:49.720
Well, it'd be a problem if he couldn't do at least that much.

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:55.270
Pay attention until the very end!

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:57.530
You'll lose everything if you make a mistake!

00:17:57.530 --> 00:17:58.650
I know!

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.980
Like I'm going to let you get away with the win!

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:02.870
Yeah.

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:06.000
We have to show him the strength of the Yokozuna of the West.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:07.450
We're counting on you, Sena!

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:07.860
Yeah.

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:12.360
<i>I'll attack him from the start and continue putting pressure on him.</i>

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:15.090
<i>He's bound to make a mistake somewhere.</i>

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:20.510
<b>The formation is set.</b>

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:22.750
<b>The final round of the Japan National ICA class...</b>

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:27.530
<b>The East-West United Final Race starts now!</b>

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:32.090
Go!  Go!  Go!

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.180
Capeta!

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:37.270
<b>The first car to make the turn is Taira, at his best today!</b>

00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:40.320
<b>He puts distance between himself and the other cars!</b>

00:18:48.070 --> 00:18:49.490
<i>What's with this guy?!</i>

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:51.950
<i>I can't even catch up to him,
let alone put pressure on him!</i>

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:57.270
<i>Wow!</i>

00:18:57.270 --> 00:18:58.860
<i>This feels great!</i>

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:00.550
<i>This is it!  This is it!</i>

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:06.720
<i>It was really good continuing to kart with everyone for these past five years!</i>

00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:12.470
<i>I can't catch up anymore.</i>

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:17.550
<i>Capeta-kun has also gone to a different world from us.</i>

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:21.390
<i>Like Naomi-senpai.</i>

00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:33.080
<b>The winner is Taira Capeta!</b>

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:35.530
<b>This is his first time in the Japan National Championship</b>

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:39.240
<b>and he finishes with a perfect pole to win!</b>

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:02.060
Ibaraki Prefecture, Yuuki District.

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:05.720
Persec Motorsports Limited.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:12.810
Is there really a racing team in the middle of these paddy fields?

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:18.630
It's here!

00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:20.800
I'm finally here!

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:26.980
Excuse me.

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:31.210
Uh...

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:34.430
Um...

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:38.880
H-Hello.

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:39.870
I'm Taira.

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:43.050
You told me I could come and have a look around, so I kindly took your offer and—

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:43.860
Wrench.

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:44.440
Huh?

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:45.780
The wrench!

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:46.730
It's over there.

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:47.690
Torque wrench.

00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:48.970
Y-Yes.

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:49.620
Uh...

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:50.600
Where is it?

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:51.800
Wrench...  Wrench...

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:53.650
What are you doing?!  Hurry up!

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:58.080
<i>Tsubomaki-san's place is famous for their Spartan training.</i>

00:20:58.080 --> 00:20:59.740
<i>Oh man...  That's right.</i>

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:02.000
Thank you.

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:06.250
Oh, thank you.

00:21:06.670 --> 00:21:09.560
Why did we let this slacker join us?

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:10.650
We can't even use him.

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:11.760
Really.

00:21:13.720 --> 00:21:19.400
<i>Can I really get on... at a place like this?</i>

00:22:50.940 --> 00:22:55.360
I'm in high school now and in the care of Persec Motorsports.

00:22:55.360 --> 00:22:56.530
Monami is a singer.

00:22:56.530 --> 00:22:58.030
Nobu is going to a new school.

00:22:58.030 --> 00:23:00.700
We've all started to walk our paths.

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:01.740
Next time, on Capeta.

00:23:01.740 --> 00:23:03.200
Next Stage!

00:23:03.200 --> 00:23:05.080
Open up the future!
